              "extmetadata": {
                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "This is \"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boulevard_du_Temple\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Boulevard du Temple\">Boulevard du Temple</a>\", the first ever photograph of a person. The photo was taken by <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Louis_Daguerre\" title=\"Louis Daguerre\">Louis Daguerre</a> in late <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=1838&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1838 (page does not exist)\">1838</a> or early <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=1839&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1839 (page does not exist)\">1839</a> in <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Paris\" title=\"Paris\">Paris</a>. It is of a busy street, but because exposure time was over ten minutes, the city traffic was moving too much to appear. The exception is a man in the bottom left corner, who stood still getting his boots polished long enough to show.",
                  "source": "commons-desc-page"
                },
